    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d844">

                <pb facs="0998" n="918" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg918"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr. Tower.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-12-31"><hi rendition="#italic">December 31,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 269.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: For your information I have to inclose
                    herewith copies of correspondence<anchor n="a" xml:id="d844-f1"/> with the
                    Russian ambassador at this capital in reference to the reported acts of the
                    United States consul at Niuchwang; also copy of the Department’s instruction to
                    Mr. Miller in the matter.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David J. Hill</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
